WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
The storm Betsy that passed in nineteen . . . was it '65 or '66?

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.480
One of those years.

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.940
Quite a few people died in that storm,

4
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.600
because they went to the attic and they didn't have the proper tools to get out through the roof.

5
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.760
And that was way past, we just used to talk about that all the time.

6
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.060
But now, we're confronted with this storm [Katrina].

7
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:27.540
So we did pull down the stairs to the attic, and I said, I told Pat, I said "I'm not going in the attic."

8
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.300
And we just laughed.

9
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.020
And just at that point, the water hit the front door.

10
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.380
Her air handler is in the hallway, right there as you're going up.

11
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:40.020
And in there is where she kept her little tools, miscellaneous tools.

12
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.760
The saw, the hammer that we needed.

13
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.580
And we got those things, and up in the attic we went!

14
00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.780
We sawed and we hammered.

15
00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:55.580
And of course, once we hewn through the roof, we could hear the helicopters passing, the orange helicopters passing.

16
00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:01.500
And we got a little flag, a towel, whatever, and we would fly it through, but nobody never stopped.

17
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.900
But we realized later that they were getting people out of the water.

18
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.780
And I guess this was my first time really praying out loud.

19
00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:16.560
And I said, "Lord, Lord, you've got to get us out of this, Lord."

20
00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.220
And just then, the boat was coming.

21
00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:19.800
Oh!

22
00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.140
Yes, just then the boat was coming.

23
00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:25.840
And he was rescuing the other people across the canal there.

24
00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.040
I yelled at the young man.

25
00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.500
I said, "Could we possibly . . . Could you possibly help us out?"

26
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.000
He said, "Oh, yes, I'll be back for you."

27
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.400
I said, "Don't tell me you're going to come back if you're not going to come back."

28
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.360
He said, "No, I wouldn't do that to you.

29
00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.500
I'll be back."

30
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.160
He said, "In about ten minutes, I'll be back.

31
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.280
Once I get all of these people out."

32
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.880
And then he came back.

33
00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:55.060
Good Samaritan, and right now I can't even think of his name, but I pray for him every night, thanking God for him every night.
